{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoVolumeConstant"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.fiveTwoShape_normSq_gt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.fiveTwoShape_normSq_gt_one","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoShapeBounds.lean#L136-L146","doc":"**`normSq y₁ > 1`, i.e. `|y₁| > 1`** — recorded because it closes the obvious\nshortcut: the `Li₂` power series does **not** converge at `y₁`, which is why the corpus\nuses the extended `cLiTwoExt`, and why a naive dilogarithm partial sum cannot be used to\nbound `VOL_5_2`. Anyone reaching for one will find it diverges. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.fiveTwoShape_im_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.fiveTwoShape_im_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoShapeBounds.lean#L115-L134","doc":"`13/10 < Im(y₁) < 132/100`. Strictly positive, and bounded away from `0` by an\nexplicit rational — which `fiveTwoShape_im_pos` alone does not give. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.radicand_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.radicand_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoShapeBounds.lean#L106-L113","doc":"The radicand is bracketed, which is what the `Im` bound needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.fiveTwoShape_re_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.fiveTwoShape_re_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoShapeBounds.lean#L98-L104","doc":"`31/40 < Re(y₁) < 4/5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.fiveTwoShape_im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.fiveTwoShape_im","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoShapeBounds.lean#L88-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.fiveTwoShape_re","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.fiveTwoShape_re","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoShapeBounds.lean#L85-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.realRoot_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.realRoot_lt","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoShapeBounds.lean#L73-L79","doc":"**Upper bracket** `t < 9/20`, from `g(9/20) > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.realRoot_gt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.realRoot_gt","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoShapeBounds.lean#L65-L71","doc":"**Lower bracket** `2/5 < t`. The cubic is strictly increasing and `g(2/5) < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.realRoot_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.realRoot_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoShapeBounds.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.realRoot_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.realRoot_pos","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoShapeBounds.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.realRoot_cubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FiveTwoShapeBounds.realRoot_cubic","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FiveTwoShapeBounds.lean#L56-L59","doc":"The defining cubic, as a standalone fact. ","signatureChunk":0}]}